{
  "explanations": [
    {
      "id": "F-D1-1b5bca2812",
      "text": "The CMDB lacks a documented dependency between ORU-CRIT-H01 and lrc-db-01 (and similar undocumented links for ORU-CRIT-H02 through ORU-CRIT-H14), observed via the interface engine for 14 days. This undocumented link means changes to lrc-db-01 could unexpectedly affect critical patient‑result interfaces, risking delayed or incorrect data for patients. The proposed fix is to add this dependency to the CMDB, as indicated by the 51 patch operations needed to remediate the drift."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D10-37ef3aa2dd",
      "text": "Backup for h02-pacs-cache-db has failed, with the last successful backup recorded on 2026-10-04. A failed backup jeopardizes the ability to restore PACS images, which could lead to loss of patient imaging data and impact care delivery. The proposed fix is to restore backup success; currently zero patch operations have been applied, indicating remediation is still needed."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-b519fcc3ae",
      "text": "Protection‑path drift is detected for h42-pacs-cache-db: the CMDB shows site H42 with backup target arr-h42-01, which deviates from the expected protection configuration. This drift could cause backups to go to an unintended site, risking loss of PACS data during a disaster and affecting patient care continuity. The proposed fix is to correct the protection settings; zero patch operations have been applied so far."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-31dd79b7d2",
      "text": "Owner drift for ris-db-01 shows a CMDB owner of NW-Imaging‑Systems while the observed owner is NW-DBA, based on five evidence records. Unclear ownership can delay incident response and hinder timely access to radiology data, affecting patient diagnosis and treatment. The proposed fix is to update the CMDB owner to the observed owner; one patch operation is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-7aa2a50db0",
      "text": "Protection‑path drift is detected for h38-pacs-cache-db: the CMDB shows site H38 with backup target arr-h38-01, deviating from the expected protection configuration. This could misdirect backups, putting PACS data at risk in a disaster and potentially affecting patient care. The proposed fix is to adjust the protection settings; zero patch operations have been applied so far."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D10-d6475e6ab6",
      "text": "Backup for h35-labmw-db has failed, with the last successful backup recorded on 2026-10-02. A failed backup risks loss of laboratory data, which could delay or impede patient diagnosis and treatment. The proposed fix is to restore backup success; currently zero patch operations have been applied."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D9-feeef47d89",
      "text": "Protection‑path drift is detected for h17-labmw-db: the CMDB shows site H17 with backup target arr-h17-01, deviating from the expected protection configuration. This could cause lab data backups to go to an unintended location, risking data loss and affecting patient care continuity. The proposed fix is to correct the protection settings; zero patch operations have been applied so far."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-fe326c7991",
      "text": "Owner drift for ie-db-01 shows a CMDB owner of NW-DBA while the observed owner is HYD-Integration-Support, based on six evidence records. This ownership mismatch can impede coordination during incidents, potentially affecting emergency‑care services and patient safety. The proposed fix is to update the CMDB owner to the observed owner; one patch operation is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D5-ebbb728ff2",
      "text": "Owner drift for lrc-db-01 shows a CMDB owner of NW-Lab-Systems while the observed owner is HYD-Integration-Support, based on eight evidence records. Unclear ownership of the lab database can delay incident response and affect timely reporting of lab results, impacting patient care. The proposed fix is to update the CMDB owner to the observed owner; one patch operation is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "F-D11-5a3435ebca",
      "text": "Data residency drift shows replication between stor-usw-01 and stor-cin-01 via pod-vol-dwh-db-01-export, indicating data may be stored outside the allowed jurisdiction. This could violate compliance requirements and expose patient data to unauthorized locations, creating legal and privacy risks. The proposed fix is to adjust the replication to meet residency rules; zero patch operations have been applied so far."
    }
  ]
}

